{"id": "q0409", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 3.01, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1799, "eot_read_ms": 25, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What is the Philly Special and when was it used ?", "transcript": "What is the Philly Special and when was it used?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The Philly Special is a trick play in American football where the quarterback throws a short pass to the running back, who then tosses it back to the quarterback in the end zone. It was famously used by the Philadelphia Eagles in Super Bowl LII on February 4, 2018, to score a game-winning touchdown against the New England Patriots.", "answer_ms": 2017}
{"id": "q0421", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 4.21, "n_chunks": 5, "n_concurrent": 5, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1032, "eot_read_ms": 25, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Explain the best way to swing a golf iron compared to a golf driver.", "transcript": "Explain the best way to swing a golf iron compared to a golf driver.", "mode": "local", "answer": "Golf drivers and irons are both clubs used in golf, but they serve very different purposes. Drivers are designed for hitting the ball long distances off the tee, typically on the first shot of a hole. They have larger clubheads with bigger \"sweet spots,\" making them easier to hit solid shots from fairways or tee boxes. Drivers produce higher ball flight and more distance because of their design and loft angle, which is usually between 8 and 12 degrees. Irons, on the other hand, are used for shorter distances and around the green. They come in various numbers like 3-iron, 5-iron, pitching wedge, etc., each with progressively less loft than the driver. Irons allow for greater control over distance and trajectory, especially useful for approach shots into the green. So, if you're hitting from the tee, use a driver; for most other shots—especially when approaching the green—use an iron depending on how far you need to hit the ball.", "answer_ms": 6352}
{"id": "q0426", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 2.9, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.11, "eot_read_ms": 27, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What is the purpose of a shot clock in basketball?", "transcript": "What is the purpose of a shot clock in basketball?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The shot clock in basketball is used to keep the game moving quickly. It limits how much time a team has to shoot the ball after gaining possession. This helps prevent teams from holding the ball for too long and keeps the pace of the game fast and exciting.", "answer_ms": 1531}
